  "title": {
    "rendered": "Seller Concessions To Buyers &#8211; How Much?"
  },
  "content": {
    "rendered": "\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Attached and Detached Resales in the Greater Phoenix Metro Area for prior 30 day period as of 2/9/19</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-ac81e17\" data-block-id=\"ac81e17\"><style>.stk-ac81e17 {box-shadow:0px 2px 20px #99999933 !important;margin-top:24px !important;margin-bottom:24px !important;}</style>\r\n<figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-7723\" src=\"https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/sellerconcessions.png\" alt=\"Chart showing seller concessions as a percentage of sale price by property price range as of February 9, 2019.\" width=\"1664\" height=\"1050\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/sellerconcessions.png 1664w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/sellerconcessions-1280x808.png 1280w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/sellerconcessions-980x618.png 980w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/sellerconcessions-480x303.png 480w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 0px) and (max-width: 480px) 480px, (min-width: 481px) and (max-width: 980px) 980px, (min-width: 981px) and (max-width: 1280px) 1280px, (min-width: 1281px) 1664px, 100vw\" /></span></figure>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The above graph represents the average seller concession to buyers within the prior 30 day period as of 2/9/2019 for closings in the Greater Phoenix Metro Market area.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-call-to-action stk-block-call-to-action stk-block stk-c6a39b5 is-style-default\" data-v=\"2\" data-block-id=\"c6a39b5\"><style>.stk-c6a39b5 {margin-top:50px !important;margin-bottom:50px !important;}</style>\r\n<div class=\"stk-block-call-to-action__content stk-content-align stk-c6a39b5-column stk-container stk-c6a39b5-container stk-hover-parent\">\r\n<div class=\"has-text-align-center stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-c6a39b5-inner-blocks\">\r\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Wondering How Much to Offer in Concessions?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-text stk-block-text stk-block stk-a32c06e\" data-block-id=\"a32c06e\"><style>.stk-a32c06e {margin-top:24px !important;}.stk-a32c06e .stk-block-text__text{line-height:1.7em !important;}</style>\r\n<p class=\"stk-block-text__text\">Seller concessions can make or break a sale. Get expert advice on offering the right amount to attract buyers and close the deal.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-button-group stk-block-button-group stk-block stk-c39ef29\" data-block-id=\"c39ef29\"><style>.stk-c39ef29 .stk-button-group{flex-direction:row !important;}@media screen and (max-width: 1023px){.stk-c39ef29 .stk-button-group{flex-direction:row !important;}}@media screen and (max-width: 767px){.stk-c39ef29 .stk-button-group{flex-direction:row !important;}}</style>\r\n<div class=\"stk-row stk-inner-blocks stk-block-content stk-button-group\">\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-button stk-block-button stk-block stk-067bcc2\" data-block-id=\"067bcc2\"><style>.stk-067bcc2 .stk-button{background:#6ca220 !important;}</style><a class=\"stk-link stk-button stk--hover-effect-darken\" href=\"#Get-in-Touch\"><span class=\"stk-button__inner-text\">Get a Free Seller Consultation</span></a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-a54f4e6\" data-block-id=\"a54f4e6\"><style>.stk-a54f4e6 {box-shadow:0px 2px 20px #99999933 !important;margin-top:24px !important;margin-bottom:24px !important;}</style>\r\n<figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-7724\" src=\"https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/closingsandconcessions.png\" alt=\"Chart showing the number of closings and the amount of concessions given to buyers as of February 9, 2019.\" width=\"1654\" height=\"1076\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/closingsandconcessions.png 1654w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/closingsandconcessions-1280x833.png 1280w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/closingsandconcessions-980x638.png 980w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/closingsandconcessions-480x312.png 480w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 0px) and (max-width: 480px) 480px, (min-width: 481px) and (max-width: 980px) 980px, (min-width: 981px) and (max-width: 1280px) 1280px, (min-width: 1281px) 1654px, 100vw\" /></span></figure>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The graph above shows the number of closings by amount of concession to the buyers in the Greater Phoenix Metro Market area. The total number of closings for the period was 2,112. Data gathered from ARMLS closings for prior 30 days as of 2/9/19</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-5a1bd68\" data-block-id=\"5a1bd68\"><style>.stk-5a1bd68 {box-shadow:0px 2px 20px #99999933 !important;margin-top:24px !important;margin-bottom:24px !important;}</style>\r\n<figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-7725\" src=\"https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/concessionsbycity.png\" alt=\"Chart showing concessions as a percentage of sale price by city as of February 9, 2019.\" width=\"1658\" height=\"1126\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/concessionsbycity.png 1658w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/concessionsbycity-1280x869.png 1280w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/concessionsbycity-980x666.png 980w, https://azmortgagebrothers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/concessionsbycity-480x326.png 480w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 0px) and (max-width: 480px) 480px, (min-width: 481px) and (max-width: 980px) 980px, (min-width: 981px) and (max-width: 1280px) 1280px, (min-width: 1281px) 1658px, 100vw\" /></span></figure>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\r\n<li><a href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/personal-finance/mortgages/article/seller-concessions-165151738.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Seller concessions to buyers</a> of single family attached and detached products ranged from a low of .9% to a high of 2.6% for 2,112 closings in the previous 30 days as of 2/9/2019 in the Greater Phoenix Metro Area.</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<li>Key cities – Gilbert had the lowest concession at 1.3% and Glendale had the highest at 2.3%</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<li>Most closings in the 30 day period – $200,000 to $300,000 price range accounted for 1,076 closings and an average seller concession to buyers of 1.9%</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<li>Anthem, Gilbert, Cave Creek, Paradise Valley averaged 1.3%</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<li>Chandler, Litchfield Park, Tempe averaged 1.5% seller concessions.</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<li>Peoria, Mesa, Sun City, averaged 1.8%.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Try us on your next loan……our clients appreciate our pricing, timing and customer service</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height: 100px;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Discover how seller concessions can benefit both parties and learn what to expect in negotiations. For more insights, check out our <a href=\"/buying-or-selling-personal-property-with-your-home-sale-must-watch-this-first/\">personal property guide</a>, find out <a href=\"/how-to-skip-2-payments-on-your-mortgage/\">how to skip two mortgage payments</a>, and review our <a href=\"/put-bow-fha-loan-gift-guide/\">FHA loan gift guide</a>.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height: 100px;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> </div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">\r\n{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\r\n  \"mainEntity\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n      \"name\": \"What are seller concessions in real estate?\",\r\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n        \"text\": \"Seller concessions are closing cost contributions from the seller to help buyers complete the purchase.\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n      \"name\": \"How much were seller concessions in Phoenix Metro?\",\r\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n        \"text\": \"Concessions ranged from 0.9% to 2.6% of sale prices across 2,112 closings in the prior 30 days as of February 9, 2019.\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Which city had the highest seller concessions?\",\r\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n        \"text\": \"Glendale recorded the highest average seller concessions at about 2.3%.\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Which price range had the most closings?\",\r\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n        \"text\": \"Homes priced between $200,000 and $300,000 had the most closings, with average concessions of 1.9%.\"\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n</script></p>",
    "protected": false
  },
